Installing and Running the Portable Agena Win32 Version
-------------------------------------------------------

If you want to use Agena on a removable drive or do not have admin rights to run the binary
Windows installer, just install this portable release.

In an NT shell, create a folder called `agena` anywhere on your drive, change into this
folder and decompress this ZIP file into it preserving the subdirectory structure of the ZIP
file, which should now look like this:

24/08/2023  12:56    <DIR>          bin         <-- includes AgenaEdit IDE
02/09/2023  08:05           687,461 change.log
18/05/2023  21:57    <DIR>          doc
24/08/2023  12:56    <DIR>          lib
25/12/2022  18:59             2,118 licence
02/09/2023  08:13             1,588 readme.w32
30/08/2023  17:08             1,021 run.bat     <-- start-up batch file
30/08/2023  17:08            36,691 run.exe     <-- alternative launcher
29/01/2023  18:48    <DIR>          share       <-- includes icons

Then create a desktop shortcut to the batch file `run.bat` or the binary launcher `run.exe` that
reside at the root of the installation. Choose an icon located in the `share\icons` folder to
beautify the shortcut. Recommendation: `agena256.ico` for Windows 2003 Server and above (e.g. XP,
Vista and later) and `agena128x128.ico` for Windows 2000/Windows 2000 Server.

Check the properties of the shortcut to be sure that the value in field "Start in" is the
path to the root Agena folder, e.g. `C:\agena`, and not to `C:\agena\bin` or anything else.

That's it. Have fun !